    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0183" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/7–943</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Churchill</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="89" xml:id="d141-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-08">July 8, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>348. I hear from Macmillan that Eisenhower and Murphy propose immediate
                    recognition of French Committee. This is rather sudden. I should like to know
                    your reactions.</p>
                <p>Our Foreign Office would also like to go ahead and recognize. My chief desire in
                    this business has been to keep in step with you.</p>
                <p>It is however essential that we should act together and that we should agree to
                    the extent and moment of our recognition.</p>
                <p>My immediately following telegram<anchor n="90" xml:id="d141-f2"/> contains
                    formula for recognition suggested by Foreign Office.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d141-f1" n="89" type="source" xml:id="d141-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of this telegram was transmitted by the British Ambassador to the Secretary
                    of State on July 9.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d141-f2" n="90" xml:id="d141-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
